---
import PageLayout from "@layouts/PageLayout.astro";
---

<PageLayout
  title="Shortcuts, Mobile & CLI API | clipboard.dulith.me"
  description="Sync your clipboard directly from iPhone Apple Shortcuts, macOS, Android HTTP Shortcuts, Tasker, or terminal curl commands using the clipboard.dulith.me REST API."
  canonicalPath="/shortcuts"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Headless Device Sync</span>
    <h1>Shortcuts &amp; CLI API</h1>
    <p>
      Push or pull clipboard text straight from iOS Share Sheet, Android Tasker, or your terminal without opening a browser tab.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="glass-card sheet">
    <div class="step-head">
      <h2>1. Public Clip API (No Auth Required)</h2>
      <span class="badge-pill ok">Open Endpoints</span>
    </div>

    <div class="well">
      <div style="font-weight:620;margin-bottom:6px;">Save text from terminal</div>
      <pre style="margin:0;overflow-x:auto;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px;"><code>curl -X POST https://clipboard.dulith.me/api/v1/clips \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '&#123;"content":"Hello from terminal","expiresIn":"1d"&#125;'</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="well">
      <div style="font-weight:620;margin-bottom:6px;">Fetch a clip or download a file</div>
      <pre style="margin:0;overflow-x:auto;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px;"><code># Read text clip
curl https://clipboard.dulith.me/api/v1/clips/CLIP_ID

# Download password-protected file
curl -H "X-Password: YOUR_PASSWORD" -OJ https://clipboard.dulith.me/api/v1/files/FILE_ID?download=1</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="glass-card sheet">
    <div class="step-head">
      <h2>2. Personal Quick Sync (Apple Shortcuts &amp; Android)</h2>
      <span class="badge-pill accent">Bearer Token</span>
    </div>

    <p style="margin:0;color:var(--label-secondary);font-size:15px;">
      Inspired by <code>YanxinTang/clipboard-online</code>, the <code>/api/v1/quick</code> endpoint stores your latest cross-device clipboard buffer in Cloudflare KV using your Worker <code>QUICK_API_TOKEN</code> secret.
    </p>

    <div class="field-grid">
      <div class="well">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:16px;">Apple Shortcuts (iOS / macOS)</h3>
        <ol style="margin:0;padding-left:18px;color:var(--label-secondary);font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;">
          <li>Create a Shortcut named <strong>Send to Clipboard</strong>.</li>
          <li>Add <strong>Get Clipboard</strong> &rarr; <strong>Get Contents of URL</strong>.</li>
          <li>URL: <code>https://clipboard.dulith.me/api/v1/quick</code>, Method: <code>POST</code>.</li>
          <li>Header: <code>Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN</code> and <code>X-Client-Name: iPhone</code>.</li>
          <li>Request Body: JSON key <code>data</code> set to Clipboard.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="well">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:16px;">Pull Latest to Device</h3>
        <pre style="margin:0;overflow-x:auto;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px;"><code># Pull latest quick clipboard
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" \
  https://clipboard.dulith.me/api/v1/quick

# Push current macOS clipboard
pbpaste | curl -X POST \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" \
  -H "X-Client-Name: MacBook" \
  --data-binary @- \
  https://clipboard.dulith.me/api/v1/quick</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
